# Frontend Performance

Performance is a production requirement.

## Server Components

Prefer React Server Components.

Use Client Components only when required.

Do not make entire pages client components unnecessarily.

## Data fetching

Avoid duplicate API requests.

Do not fetch the same data independently in multiple child components when it can be shared.

## Images

Use Next.js image optimization where applicable.

Provide:

- width
- height
- appropriate sizing
- meaningful alt text

Avoid loading unnecessarily large images.

## Lists

For large lists:

- paginate
- virtualize where appropriate
- avoid rendering unnecessary records

## Bundle size

Do not add dependencies without justification.

Prefer existing project utilities.

Avoid importing entire libraries when only a small function is required.

## Rendering

Avoid unnecessary re-renders.

Do not use memoization blindly.

Optimize only when there is a demonstrated need.

## Loading

Use:

- streaming
- Suspense
- skeletons
- progressive loading

where appropriate.

## Admin dashboard

Do not load every analytics dataset on initial page load.

Load expensive dashboard sections independently where appropriate.

## AI interface

Do not render entire conversation history unnecessarily when conversations become large.

Use pagination or virtualization when required.

## Monitoring

Important frontend errors should be observable in production through the application's error-monitoring strategy.